# .secrets-allowlist — canon repo
# Narrow, documented exceptions to the secret-scrub pre-commit gate.
# Each line is a regex matched against the FULL line; matching lines skip scanning.

# CANON hash-chain fields: "hash" and "prev_hash" are SHA-256 content hashes
# (64 lowercase hex) computed deterministically over the public record bytes.
# They are integrity data, not secrets — they cannot be "rotated" or "vaulted"
# without destroying the chain.
# Residual risk (documented, accepted): the allowlist is checked per line
# BEFORE the pattern scans, so a line carrying both a chain hash and a
# real secret-looking token would be skipped. Accepted because every record
# line is machine-generated through the schema-validated CLI (unknown fields
# rejected), and no human hand-edits the JSONL; see
# CANON-FREEZE-2026-10-08.md known imperfections.
"(prev_)?hash":"[0-9a-f]{64}"
# Same rationale for context receipt hashes quoted in docs: deterministic
# public integrity data, not secrets.
context_hash: [0-9a-f]{64}
# RFC-002 doc prose (pre-existing §§30/53, 2026-10-08 wave-4): long
# slash-separated API-surface enumerations read as high-entropy runs to
# LONG_PAT. This is documentation of the MCP/organelle interface
# vocabulary — not credentials. Scoped to the exact doc lines.
^canon\.context/get/search/
pl\.assert/verify/
states OPEN/IN_PROGRESS/
^Decomposable: canon-parser/
